            "pageCount": 1,
            "processed": true,
            "summary": "This article presents a case study of a 71-year-old woman who experienced dizziness and a fall shortly after beginning treatment with Sedaprin, a medication prescribed for sleep difficulties. The patient was started on a 10mg nightly dosage but reported dizziness upon standing just two days later, leading to a fall and a bruise on her hip. After discontinuing Sedaprin, the patient did not experience any further falls in the following month. \n\nThe authors emphasize that the orthostatic effects of Sedaprin may often be overlooked in older adults, suggesting that lower starting doses might be more appropriate for this age group to minimize risks. This document is relevant to a patient-safety review because it highlights potential adverse effects associated with Sedaprin in elderly patients, which is important information for monitoring drug safety. The case underlines the need for caution in prescribing this medication to older adults and could inform guidelines for safer prescribing practices."
        }
    ],
